# Angular Rules

- Use modern Angular, not legacy AngularJS 1.x.
- Prefer standalone components and the project's established Angular conventions.
- Keep components focused on presentation/orchestration; move reusable business/data logic to services.
- Reuse existing components, directives, pipes, models and services before creating new ones.
- Avoid duplicate API calls and duplicate state models.
- Keep POS screens optimized for keyboard/scanner workflows.
- Minimize visible controls and unnecessary navigation.
- Keep forms short and use clear validation/error states.
- Do not add a UI library unless approved.
- Follow the existing project design tokens and component patterns once established.
